/// All four male coveralls (Blue, Brn, Gray, Orange) are duplicates of one mesh (identical vertices and triangles), so this one table serves all of them.
///
/// One record per triangle of the imported mesh, Stride floats each: hideFlag (1 = may hide), then the triangle's centroid in mesh space (x, y, z;
/// mesh space = the Blender local axes: x = left/right, y = front/back with the character facing -Y, z = up). The runtime classifies each torso triangle
/// by the NEAREST record (see ModularAvatarAssembler.MaskSaysHideMale), so it stays correct even if the exporter splits a quad the other way.
/// Note: every face in these meshes exists TWICE at the same position (Blender shows 230 positions x 2 coincident faces); Tad's selection covers one
/// copy of each, so a position counts as "hide" when either copy was selected - hiding only one copy would change nothing visible.
/// Regenerate by re-selecting faces in Blender, saving, and re-running the extraction (see the 2026-10-10 notes in CLAUDE.md).
